```c
if (sk->sk_bound_dev_if || exact_dif) {
    bool dev_match = (sk->sk_bound_dev_if == dif || sk->sk_bound_dev_if == sdif);
    if (exact_dif && !dev_match)
        return -1;
    if (sk->sk_bound_dev_if && dev_match)
        score += 4;
}
```
Reason:
The condition `if (!dev_match)` allowed for a mismatch in the device interface (dif) when `sk_bound_dev_if` was non-null, which broke the expected behavior of `SO_BINDTODEVICE` by not enforcing a strict match, leading to incorrect socket behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (!dev_match)
    return -1;
```
Reason:
This change enforces that any mismatch in the device interface (dif) is now fatal, restoring the original semantics of `SO_BINDTODEVICE` by ensuring that the device match must be strictly enforced, thus preventing incorrect socket behavior.

